    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "view-placement-sheet",
      "x": 5440,
      "y": 7264,
      "name": "Component / View placement",
      "width": 560,
      "fill": "$--card",
      "cornerRadius": "$--radius-md",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$--spacing-lg",
      "padding": "$--spacing-md",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "view-placement-sheet-title",
          "name": "Title block",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": "$--spacing-xxs",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "view-placement-sheet-title-name",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$--foreground",
              "content": "View placement (web Workspace)",
              "fontFamily": "$--font-ui",
              "fontSize": "$--text-title",
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "view-placement-sheet-title-spec",
              "name": "Spec",
              "fill": "$--subtle-foreground",
              "content": "Where a dragged view will land. Over a tab bar, the insertion line (--size-tab-indicator wide in --color-accent, the tab bar's height) marks the slot: its own bar reorders, another area's bar moves the view there with no split and no copy. Over an edge of an area's content, the split overlay washes the half of that area the drop would create (--color-selected-wash inside a hairline --color-accent boundary) with one short label, and the drop creates that area and moves the view into it. One destination at a time. An ineligible target (the area cannot be halved at its minimum, the Workspace is at its area or depth limit, or it is not a View area) draws no overlay and the pointer shows the forbidden cursor. Escape, an outside release and a vanished target keep the original layout; nothing resizes during the drag and the preview is never stored. The edge zone size is the implementation's.",
              "fontFamily": "$--font-ui",
              "fontSize": "$--text-caption",
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "view-placement-sheet-master",
          "name": "Master",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": "$--spacing-xs",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "view-placement-sheet-master-name",
              "name": "State name",
              "fill": "$--muted-foreground",
              "content": "Masters - the insertion line and the split overlay; the examples below place refs",
              "fontFamily": "$--font-ui",
              "fontSize": "$--text-micro",
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "view-placement-sheet-masters",
              "name": "Masters",
              "gap": "$--spacing-lg",
              "alignItems": "center",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "view-insertion-line",
                  "name": "Component / View insertion line",
                  "reusable": true,
                  "width": 2,
                  "height": 32,
                  "fill": "$--primary"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "view-split-overlay",
                  "name": "Component / View split overlay",
                  "reusable": true,
                  "width": 240,
                  "height": 160,
                  "fill": "$--color-selected-wash",
                  "stroke": "$--primary",
                  "strokeWidth": "$--size-hairline",
                  "strokeAlignment": "inner",
